The trifecta.

1364
00:51:23.540 --> 00:51:24.440
Holy cow!

1365
00:51:24.820 --> 00:51:25.300
All three.

1366
00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:26.920
Not on Monk.

1367
00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:28.180
Not on Monk.

1368
00:51:28.580 --> 00:51:29.660
There's still room.

1369
00:51:29.840 --> 00:51:30.440
There's still room.

1370
00:51:30.540 --> 00:51:33.840
Future guest star, if you could be on all three Law & Orders and Monk,

1371
00:51:33.960 --> 00:51:35.940
I'm going to drive to your house and give you a cake.

1372
00:51:37.680 --> 00:51:42.480
So, when I was trading emails with Rob, I was like, Rob, you've got to share what it was like in that room

1373
00:51:43.100 --> 00:51:45.880
when Steve, as Michael, is falling apart.

1374
00:51:46.180 --> 00:51:46.540
Yes.

1375
00:51:46.940 --> 00:51:48.260
And singling you out.

1376
00:51:48.780 --> 00:51:49.820
I mean, I don't know.

1377
00:51:49.900 --> 00:51:50.620
How did you do that?

1378
00:51:50.680 --> 00:51:51.600
How did you get through it?

1379
00:51:51.600 --> 00:51:52.720
And here's what he had to say.

1380
00:51:53.180 --> 00:52:02.260
My memories of shooting that scene in the conference room with Steve are mostly about just trying not to laugh

1381
00:52:02.260 --> 00:52:13.720
because sometimes I just start laughing when people are funny because, really, I feel like a lot of times on comedy shows,

1382
00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:17.580
you're trying to make the other person laugh.

1383
00:52:17.580 --> 00:52:21.380
In a way, you're kind of trying to f*** with them a little bit.

1384
00:52:21.620 --> 00:52:28.840
So, anyway, I was just trying to keep a straight face because Steve is so funny and Jenna is so funny

1385
00:52:28.840 --> 00:52:30.540
and everybody on the show is so funny.

1386
00:52:30.620 --> 00:52:31.920
And I also get very nervous.

1387
00:52:31.920 --> 00:52:39.700
I get nervous going into a new show and, you know, there's this whole other culture there already established.

1388
00:52:39.700 --> 00:52:44.940
When you're a guest actor on a show, it's different because you don't know what you're walking into.

1389
00:52:45.300 --> 00:52:49.620
So, I was a little bit nervous and Steve is just, you know, iconic.

1390
00:52:49.900 --> 00:52:51.060
Steve is just so funny.

1391
00:52:51.300 --> 00:53:01.740
And when he's kind of coming at me like that, he's, you know, putting me down and ignoring me and calling me names in a very funny way.

1392
00:53:01.920 --> 00:53:04.740
But it's all so funny.

1393
00:53:04.820 --> 00:53:06.960
So, mostly trying not to laugh.

1394
00:53:07.980 --> 00:53:12.440
I loved his description of what it's like to be a guest actor on a show.

1395
00:53:13.020 --> 00:53:20.000
Walking into the world and it's a comedy and it's supposed to be funny, but then you're not supposed to laugh.

1396
00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:22.800
I just, I related to all of that so much.

1397
00:53:22.960 --> 00:53:23.520
I did too.

1398
00:53:23.520 --> 00:53:29.040
Well, we also asked him, does he still get recognized as AJ?

1399
00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:32.520
He's been on, what did you say, 140?

1400
00:53:33.120 --> 00:53:35.560
140 movies and TV shows.

1401
00:53:35.880 --> 00:53:37.600
Does he get recognized as AJ?

1402
00:53:37.900 --> 00:53:38.880
Let's find out.

1403
00:53:39.580 --> 00:53:43.480
Do I get recognized as AJ from The Office?

1404
00:53:43.480 --> 00:53:45.280
Are you kidding me?

1405
00:53:45.280 --> 00:53:46.020
Yes.

1406
00:53:47.500 --> 00:53:48.580
Yes, a lot.

1407
00:53:48.740 --> 00:53:50.880
And I'm so thankful for it.

1408
00:53:50.940 --> 00:53:53.980
It is very fun to be recognized.

1409
00:53:54.060 --> 00:53:59.380
No matter what people tell you, it is fun because it's, you know, it's people love it.

1410
00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:03.000
They love the show and that's fun.

1411
00:54:03.260 --> 00:54:09.320
You know, like everyone had an opinion about Michael and Holly's relationship and I was just standing in the way.

1412
00:54:09.480 --> 00:54:11.240
So, I would get threatened by strangers.

1413
00:54:11.240 --> 00:54:13.320
You know, it was crazy.

1414
00:54:13.560 --> 00:54:16.580
In fact, people used to come up to me out of the blue.

1415
00:54:16.820 --> 00:54:24.060
I remember people would sometimes whisper in my ear, like come up behind me and say, you stay away from Holly.

1416
00:54:24.280 --> 00:54:25.740
You stay away from Holly.

1417
00:54:26.240 --> 00:54:30.600
And what's crazy is that my wife in real life, her name is Holly.

1418
00:54:30.600 --> 00:54:41.480
So, I would have to decide in about two seconds, okay, is this someone that used to date my wife in real life that I should murder?

1419
00:54:41.980 --> 00:54:46.720
Or is this just a fan of The Office acting like a creeper?

1420
00:54:47.580 --> 00:54:50.140
I love that his wife's name is Holly.

1421
00:54:50.380 --> 00:54:51.020
I know!

1422
00:54:51.220 --> 00:54:52.020
That's insane.

1423
00:54:52.260 --> 00:54:56.140
That is crazy though that people go up to him and they're like, leave Holly alone.

1424
00:54:56.340 --> 00:54:57.160
And he's like, wait, what?

1425
00:54:57.160 --> 00:54:58.200
Wait, wait, that's my wife.

1426
00:54:58.280 --> 00:54:59.940
Oh, you're, oh, okay.

1427
00:55:00.100 --> 00:55:01.060
Oh, I know what you are.

1428
00:55:01.400 --> 00:55:01.760
Amazing.

1429
00:55:02.220 --> 00:55:04.840
Well, thank you, Rob, for sending in your audio clips.

1430
00:55:04.980 --> 00:55:06.080
It was so nice of you.

1431
00:55:06.240 --> 00:55:07.800
I love listening to your voice.

1432
00:55:08.040 --> 00:55:10.000
I think he has a soothing, pleasant voice.

1433
00:55:10.340 --> 00:55:11.780
Rob, she's not kidding.

1434
00:55:11.980 --> 00:55:18.300
While we were recording this episode and you sent in your audio clips, Jenna was like, I just love the sound of his voice.

1435
00:55:18.300 --> 00:55:18.860
I know.

1436
00:55:18.860 --> 00:55:23.000
I hope you get tons of voiceover work because I would buy anything you're selling.

1437
00:55:23.600 --> 00:55:24.020
Hey!

1438
00:55:24.360 --> 00:55:24.600
Yeah.

1439
00:55:24.800 --> 00:55:25.840
How about them apples?

1440
00:55:26.600 --> 00:55:29.000
So, Jenna, Michael has left.

1441
00:55:29.520 --> 00:55:30.460
Pam is in charge.

1442
00:55:30.860 --> 00:55:34.000
She goes right into Forrest Gump.

1443
00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:39.800
Lady, this was one of my favorite shooting days ever, having to take over the presentation.

1444
00:55:40.100 --> 00:55:41.880
It was so fun to watch you.

1445
00:55:42.020 --> 00:55:42.900
It was hilarious.

1446
00:55:43.280 --> 00:55:47.340
I loved watching Pam try to do Michael's movie bits.

1447
00:55:47.780 --> 00:55:49.700
Angela, you know I'm not great with accents.

1448
00:55:49.960 --> 00:55:50.920
I know this.

1449
00:55:51.020 --> 00:55:51.720
Or impressions.

1450
00:55:51.720 --> 00:55:57.420
I cannot tell you how hard I worked on that Forrest Gump voice.

1451
00:55:57.920 --> 00:55:59.200
Oh, my gosh, lady.

1452
00:55:59.460 --> 00:56:00.260
So hard.

1453
00:56:00.500 --> 00:56:03.580
Lady, I thought you were doing a bit to be bad, right?

1454
00:56:04.040 --> 00:56:04.600
Yes.

1455
